From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Misaka0x272F <324347816+Misaka0x272F@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: support UGREEN a69c:88de (AIC8800DC variant)

The UGREEN AX300 (CM760) leaves USB mass-storage mode as
a69c:88de and reports "Product: AIC8800DC". That PID is absent from
aicwf_usb_id_table[], so the driver never probes it.

Add it the same way shenmintao/aic8800dc commit 46003a1 does: append it
to the existing AIC8800DC branch in aicwf_usb_chipmatch() and to its
USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO entry, rather than adding a separate case
with plain USB_DEVICE. The interface-class match stays consistent with
the sibling entries, which matters because the device exposes more than
one interface.

The PID define is placed after 0x88dd so the list stays ordered by hex
value, and is added to both CONFIG_USB_BT branches: aicwf_usb_chipmatch()
is not guarded by that option and references the symbol unconditionally,
so it has to be defined whichever branch the build selects.

Firmware: no new files are needed. The 8800DC path uses fixed names
(aic_userconfig_8800dc.txt, aic_powerlimit_8800dc.txt,
fmacfw_patch_8800dc*.bin, fmacfw_calib_8800dc*.bin), not per-VID
calibration, and all of them are already shipped under
src/USB/driver_fw/fw/aic8800DC/. Mapping 0x88de to PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DC
therefore reuses the existing firmware set.

Signed-off-by: Misaka0x272F <324347816+Misaka0x272F@users.noreply.github.com>
---
.../drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.c       |    3 ++-
 .../drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.h       |    2 ++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
---
diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.c
index b3e194b..e677d06 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.c
@@ -2339,7 +2339,7 @@ static int aicwf_usb_chipmatch(struct aic_usb_dev *usb_dev, u16_l vid, u16_l pid
 		usb_dev->chipid = PRODUCT_ID_AIC8801;
 		AICWFDBG(LOGINFO, "%s USE AIC8801\r\n", __func__);
 		return 0;
-	}else if(pid == USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DC){
+	}else if(pid == USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DC || pid == USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DE){
 		usb_dev->chipid = PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DC;
 		AICWFDBG(LOGINFO, "%s USE AIC8800DC\r\n", __func__);
 		return 0;
@@ -2657,6 +2657,7 @@ static struct usb_device_id aicwf_usb_id_table[] = {
     {USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D81, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff)},
     {USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D41, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff)},
     {USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DC, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff)},
+    {USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DE, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff)},
     {USB_DEVICE(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DW)},
     {USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC_V2, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D81X2, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff)},
     {USB_DEVICE(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC_V2, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D89X2)},
diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.h b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.h
index 7353999..d9e4b35 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.h
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.h
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8801          0x8801
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DC        0x88dc
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DW        0x88dd
+#define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DE        0x88de
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D81       0x8d81
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D81X2     0x8d91
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D89X2     0x8d99
@@ -30,6 +31,7 @@
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8801          0x8801
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DC        0x88dc
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DW        0x88dd
+#define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DE        0x88de
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D81       0x8d81
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D41       0x8d41
 #define USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D81X2     0x8d91
